In a discussion about a perspectives piece titled "Bridging Research and Policy to Achieve a Beneficial Clean Energy Future in the United States," James Rising sought advice on where to submit the manuscript after rejections from Joule and One Earth. The piece highlights the success of clean energy due to technological advancements and policy advocacy but emphasizes the ongoing reliance on fossil fuels. I suggested several alternative journals for submission, including Energy Policy, Renewable and Sustainable Energy Reviews, Energy Research & Social Science, Global Environmental Change, Environmental Science & Policy, Climate Policy, and Nature Energy. I advised James to emphasize the interdisciplinary and collaborative nature of the work in his cover letter to enhance its appeal, encouraging persistence in finding the right publication venue.
